# msesh presets — copy to ~/.config/msesh/presets.conf and edit.
#
# One `name = command` per line. These override the built-ins of the same name,
# so redefining `claude` here changes what a bare `msesh build 4` launches.
#
# A preset whose command runs claude is detected as a claude pane: it gets
# --effort injected when you pass -e, and it is what --lazy leaves pre-typed
# rather than started. Everything else is run as-is.
#
# `msesh preset list` shows what is currently defined, built-ins first;
# `msesh preset edit` opens this file; `msesh help preset` explains the rest.

# --- built-ins, shown here so you can see the shape ---------------------------
# claude = claude --remote-control --dangerously-skip-permissions
# cly    = claude --remote-control --dangerously-skip-permissions
# plan   = claude --remote-control --permission-mode plan
# safe   = claude --remote-control
# bash   = bash -i          (also: sh)
# pwsh   = powershell.exe -NoLogo   (also: ps)
# cmd    = cmd.exe

# --- your own ----------------------------------------------------------------
# A claude pane that starts in a specific repo:
# work = cd /c/Users/me/projects/thing && claude --remote-control

# A pane that watches a build:
# watch = npm run dev

# A pane for logs:
# logs = tail -f /var/log/whatever.log
